investigative powers to counter hybrid threats. Meanwhile, German inflation rose as the ECB reconsiders interest rates. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz, Weidel face off after AfD state win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4cd7afb758593197dffdbe05f1ee8e422bfaec65efe27ff676acd8f475977dae</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-weidel-face-off-after-afd-state-win/live-79196246--7057d0c40f30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-weidel-face-off-after-afd-state-win/live-79196246?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alice Weidel and Friedrich Merz traded barbs in the Bundestag days after the AfD's victory in Saxony-Anhalt put new pressure on the German chancellor.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the September 11, 2001 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff2544e775e5f4750f7697ddc74e9c7596a55ce94bcac64ec4100d693883201f</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918--22a07e00351f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 attacks were partly planned in Hamburg, via the so-called Hamburg cell, whose members played key roles in the plot. A look back at a day that shook up Germany’s approach to national security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>BSW and AfD – a political love-hate relationship in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a11682e391b096ddf6acd033994121926b2506602db2085d2a117531b5d76ad0</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T13:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bsw-and-afd-a-political-love-hate-relationship-in-germany/a-79185782--2f6a7962abcf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bsw-and-afd-a-political-love-hate-relationship-in-germany/a-79185782?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Sahra Wagenknecht Alliance (BSW) could help the Alternative for Germany (AfD) into power in Saxony-Anhalt. But the BSW is riddled with infighting</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9fdb2404e0224d54167320cc5adda56cdfad936ca6f8aa9bc66f64c0cee64c7</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c777745376a259b01095507fe728c3ed333df3f05fffb31ca46cc771cafe938</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4765e6e6fad7586d29435c2658a2374d09b1ecddc0a542b7f9c814c2fb9465ab</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--1ca180b39c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
